    "collapsible_tabs_UDrTRf": {
      "type": "collapsible-tabs",
      "blocks": {
        "content_aq3BG8": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "What is a GVM upgrade and why do I need one?",
            "content": "<p>Gross Vehicle Mass (GVM) is the maximum your Chevy Silverado 1500 can legally weigh when fully loaded—including the truck, passengers, fuel, accessories (like bull bars and canopies), and tow ball weight. If you are towing heavy or building a touring rig, the factory payload gets eaten up fast. Our GVM upgrades legally increase this limit so you can carry your gear without voiding your insurance or risking hefty fines.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "content_97RYwd": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "What does \"Pre-Rego\" and \"SSM Approval\" mean?",
            "content": "<p>SSM stands for Second Stage of Manufacture. When we upgrade your truck <em>before</em> it is registered for the very first time (Pre-Rego), the federal government recognizes ORI as the secondary manufacturer. This means your massive lift, larger tyres, and upgraded GVM are baked into the truck's federal compliance plate. It is 100% legal to drive and insure in every state and territory in Australia.<br/><br/></p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "content_k7yrdM": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Will upgrading my GVM reduce my towing capacity?",
            "content": "<p>Not with an ORI package. The LTZ stages, Stage 1 and Stage 3, hold the full 4500kg braked towing capacity. The ZR2 stages, Stage 2 and Stage 4, are rated to 4200kg, which is what the ZR2 tows from the factory, so nothing is lost there either.</p><p>Gross Combined Mass lifts from the factory 7160kg to 8150kg on Stages 1 and 2. Stages 3 and 4 keep the factory 7160kg GCM, because those builds spend their allowance on the six-inch lift and 37-inch tyres rather than on combined mass.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "content_rQQeBN": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Are 35-inch and 37-inch tyres actually legal on these builds?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. Stage 1 and Stage 2 are federally engineered for 35x12.5 R18 or 35x12.5 R20 tyres, and Stage 3 and Stage 4 step up to 37x12.5 R18 or 37x12.5 R20. Every size is certified as part of the build when done Pre-Rego under our SSM approval.</p><p>No state-based engineering headaches, just turn the key and drive it legally anywhere in the country.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "content_aq3BG8",
        "content_97RYwd",
        "content_k7yrdM",
        "content_rQQeBN"
      ],
